{
 "note": "The store catalog for the clut corpus: what this shop sells, as a text list. The photo path retrieves against it by text (server/src/catalog.ts) instead of by image, so it runs without a GPU and without the Python stack. Entries are what a resolver may name; a product not in this list is one the resolver must decline rather than approximate.",
 "provenance": "Written by hand on 2026-09-09. No image and no licensed dataset: the entries are product names and brands, taken from what is legible in the fifteen photographs of corpus/clut/manifest.json plus the same brands' publicly listed ranges. 'truth' marks an entry a photograph actually contains, and is metadata for the harness only; it is never shown to a model and never read by the resolver.",
 "why_distractors": "A catalog holding only the answers would measure nothing: every query would have exactly one plausible target. Distractors are chosen adversarially, mostly siblings in the same brand's range (Barilla spaghetti beside thick spaghetti and thin spaghetti; Priano rigatoni beside penne rigate and bucatini), because naming the range but not the variety is the failure this resolver exists to catch.",
 "counts": {
  "entries": 250,
  "truth": 48,
  "brands": 41
 },
